<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 321.2 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 321.2 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of December 26 raised 321.2 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 428.3 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 124.7 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.29 (14.29)	   55.2 (40.4)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.15 (16.21)	   49. (43.6)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.02 (17.16)	   61.8 (122.0)</p>
<p>    24 months		 19.58 (20.04)	  155.2 (222.3)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,552 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,552.25 a week earlier and 1,596 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
